 @TheRedRaven_  Idk why, crypto-mining isn’t evil. If you have a scalped card, you should be cryptomining to get some of that income back.

In fact, ironically, if everyone who hated cryptominers for hogging cards would start crypto-mining, it’d be far less profitable to hog cards, de-incentivizing cryptomining farms to hog them. Because the amount of crypto you get is dependent on the difficulty (yield for the same amount of compute power) of the network. If everyone with an rx580 8gb, or a 1060 6gb who’s complaining about large crypto-mining operations, decided to start mining, they’d probably get an MSRP upgrade faster, and they’d also have some pocket-change to pay for a portion of the new card that a crypto-farm would have otherwise scooped up.

Gamers could literally rise-up against the crypto-mining farms to get cheaper GPUs, but they don’t get how crypto works.

